WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:02.135
Ukraine is attempting to regroup

00:00:02.135 --> 00:00:03.169
after Russia launched

00:00:03.169 --> 00:00:04.537
its largest missile barrage

00:00:04.537 --> 00:00:05.505
so far this year.

00:00:05.505 --> 00:00:07.240
95 missiles

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:08.842
over the course of just the past day.

00:00:08.842 --> 00:00:10.443
Ukraine's military says it was only able

00:00:10.443 --> 00:00:11.945
to intercept about a third of them.

00:00:11.945 --> 00:00:13.646
34 in Kiev.

00:00:13.646 --> 00:00:15.648
Power and water have now been restored.

00:00:15.648 --> 00:00:17.517
But, boy, it was a tough night.

00:00:17.517 --> 00:00:18.485
Yeah, absolutely.

00:00:18.485 --> 00:00:19.619
We are also watching

00:00:19.619 --> 00:00:20.987
an event happening in Kiev right now.

00:00:20.987 --> 00:00:22.255
It's a burial service

00:00:22.255 --> 00:00:23.757
that's being held for a fallen

00:00:23.757 --> 00:00:24.691
Ukrainian commander

00:00:24.691 --> 00:00:25.925
who was killed in Baku.

00:00:25.925 --> 00:00:27.927
CNN's Ivan Watson is there.

00:00:27.927 --> 00:00:28.862
So, Ivan,

00:00:28.862 --> 00:00:31.398
what more do we know about this commander

00:00:34.567 --> 00:00:35.035
right.

00:00:35.035 --> 00:00:35.635
Well,

00:00:35.635 --> 00:00:37.137
this young man's name was Dmytro

00:00:37.137 --> 00:00:37.904
Katsav Bylo.

00:00:37.904 --> 00:00:40.840
He went by the codename Da Vinci.

00:00:41.241 --> 00:00:44.878
And part of his funeral is taking place

00:00:45.211 --> 00:00:45.612
here.

00:00:45.612 --> 00:00:46.579
We've been watching

00:00:46.579 --> 00:00:49.249
funeral and memorial events in Kiev

00:00:49.916 --> 00:00:51.418
for hours now.

00:00:51.418 --> 00:00:53.253
The church service was actually attended

00:00:53.253 --> 00:00:54.054
by the Ukrainian

00:00:54.054 --> 00:00:55.622
president, Volodymyr Zelensky,

00:00:55.622 --> 00:00:58.458
and the top military command were in

00:00:58.758 --> 00:01:01.294
Kiev's Maidan, that central square

00:01:01.961 --> 00:01:04.230
where thousands gathered

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:05.198
to pay their respects

00:01:05.198 --> 00:01:05.732
to this man

00:01:05.732 --> 00:01:06.199
who was killed

00:01:06.199 --> 00:01:06.800
this week

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:09.602
in the grinding battle of Mahmoud,

00:01:09.602 --> 00:01:11.571
that small southeastern

00:01:11.571 --> 00:01:12.705
Ukrainian city

00:01:12.705 --> 00:01:13.740
where the Russian

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:15.208
and Ukrainian militaries

00:01:15.208 --> 00:01:17.143
are pounding each other day

00:01:17.143 --> 00:01:17.744
after day

00:01:17.744 --> 00:01:20.814
for months now for control of that city.

00:01:21.381 --> 00:01:23.950
Now, this man, Da Vinci, as he's

00:01:23.950 --> 00:01:25.952
known last year, Zelensky,

00:01:25.952 --> 00:01:27.387
the Ukrainian president,

00:01:27.387 --> 00:01:28.388
gave him the honor,

00:01:28.388 --> 00:01:31.458
calling him a hero of Ukraine.

00:01:31.991 --> 00:01:34.561
And he is viewed by many of the people

00:01:34.561 --> 00:01:35.862
who the thousands have gathered

00:01:35.862 --> 00:01:37.130
as a national hero,

00:01:37.130 --> 00:01:38.798
someone who participated

00:01:38.798 --> 00:01:40.767
in the 2014 protests

00:01:42.635 --> 00:01:44.270
the 2014 protests

00:01:44.270 --> 00:01:46.473
against a pro-Russian president

00:01:46.473 --> 00:01:48.241
in the Maidan Square

00:01:48.241 --> 00:01:49.642
that ultimately resulted

00:01:49.642 --> 00:01:51.311
in the overthrow of that president.

00:01:51.311 --> 00:01:53.113
He fled to neighboring Russia.

00:01:53.113 --> 00:01:53.847
So

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:57.117
da Vinci had been a young activist there

00:01:57.283 --> 00:01:58.418
and then joined

00:01:58.418 --> 00:01:59.119
a militia

00:01:59.119 --> 00:02:00.053
that fought against

00:02:00.053 --> 00:02:01.454
pro-Russian separatists

00:02:01.454 --> 00:02:02.856
in the Donbass region

00:02:02.856 --> 00:02:04.190
for years after that,

00:02:04.190 --> 00:02:06.025
and then has been part of

00:02:06.025 --> 00:02:07.260
the armed forces

00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:09.762
fighting against the Russian invasion

00:02:09.963 --> 00:02:11.397
over the course of the last year.

00:02:11.397 --> 00:02:12.899
He is the youngest battalion

00:02:12.899 --> 00:02:15.401
commander in the Ukrainian armed forces.

00:02:16.035 --> 00:02:18.505
The crowds have been chanting things like

00:02:19.506 --> 00:02:21.708
heroes never die.

00:02:21.708 --> 00:02:23.476
And I think this underscores

00:02:23.476 --> 00:02:25.211
the immense sacrifice

00:02:25.211 --> 00:02:27.480
that Ukrainian military

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:30.250
commanders are paying in this battle.

00:02:30.550 --> 00:02:32.452
This contest, this deadly contest

00:02:32.452 --> 00:02:34.220
against the Russian military

00:02:34.220 --> 00:02:35.622
in parliament.

00:02:35.622 --> 00:02:36.723
Back to you.

00:02:36.723 --> 00:02:37.590
Ivan Watson

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:38.625
live for us there this morning.

00:02:38.625 --> 00:02:39.726
Ivan, appreciate it. Thank you.

00:02:41.528 --> 00:02:42.462
Let's dove deeper in all of

00:02:42.462 --> 00:02:43.596
this now with retired Brigadier

00:02:43.596 --> 00:02:44.397
General Mark Kimmitt.

00:02:44.397 --> 00:02:45.832
Good to have you on, sir.

00:02:45.932 --> 00:02:46.499
Let's talk

00:02:46.499 --> 00:02:47.400
first about this missile

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:48.268
barrage overnight.

00:02:48.268 --> 00:02:49.769
One, it's the scope

00:02:49.769 --> 00:02:50.970
hit across the nation.

00:02:50.970 --> 00:02:51.771
Even killing people

00:02:51.771 --> 00:02:52.172
all the way

00:02:52.172 --> 00:02:54.874
in the western part of the country

00:02:54.874 --> 00:02:56.509
seems to be a mix of a couple of things.

00:02:56.509 --> 00:02:57.944
Hypersonic missiles,

00:02:57.944 --> 00:02:59.312
difficult to impossible to shoot down

00:02:59.312 --> 00:03:01.080
with Ukrainian air defenses,

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:03.683
but also these Iranian Shihad drones.

00:03:03.683 --> 00:03:05.685
And it seems fired at the same time.

00:03:05.685 --> 00:03:06.953
Is that by designed

00:03:06.953 --> 00:03:08.955
to overwhelm Ukraine's air defenses?

00:03:08.955 --> 00:03:09.889
Sure. Absolutely.

00:03:09.889 --> 00:03:11.791
And it's their version of shock

00:03:11.791 --> 00:03:12.392
and awe to

00:03:12.392 --> 00:03:14.360
they're trying to make a huge effect

00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:16.563
on the population and the infrastructure.

00:03:16.930 --> 00:03:19.465
And are Ukrainian air defenses

00:03:19.465 --> 00:03:21.768
even with the addition of more advanced

00:03:21.801 --> 00:03:23.670
Western NATO's systems

00:03:23.670 --> 00:03:25.271
still overwhelm there by these

00:03:25.271 --> 00:03:26.372
these Russian missiles?

00:03:26.372 --> 00:03:26.773
They are

00:03:26.773 --> 00:03:28.708
I think until we see the patriot

00:03:28.708 --> 00:03:30.243
get on to the ground

00:03:30.243 --> 00:03:31.244
or they're going to

00:03:31.244 --> 00:03:32.312
be on their back foot,

00:03:32.312 --> 00:03:33.613
especially when you send

00:03:33.613 --> 00:03:35.882
so many at once, it's

00:03:35.882 --> 00:03:37.083
hard to target all of them,

00:03:37.083 --> 00:03:38.518
hard to shoot them all down.

00:03:38.518 --> 00:03:39.285
Another thing

00:03:39.285 --> 00:03:40.620
this is CNN's reporting

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:41.087
is that

00:03:41.087 --> 00:03:42.422
Russia is capturing

00:03:42.422 --> 00:03:44.657
some Western made us supplied

00:03:44.657 --> 00:03:45.992
in particular weapons

00:03:45.992 --> 00:03:46.559
in the

00:03:46.559 --> 00:03:47.193
in this fight

00:03:47.193 --> 00:03:48.428
so far, including the javelin

00:03:48.428 --> 00:03:49.562
anti-tank missile

00:03:49.562 --> 00:03:50.496
and the Stinger shoulder

00:03:50.496 --> 00:03:52.432
fired anti-aircraft missile,

00:03:52.432 --> 00:03:54.901
sending them to Iran, in effect,

00:03:54.901 --> 00:03:56.102
as a gift

00:03:56.102 --> 00:03:58.238
for them to reverse engineer

00:03:58.238 --> 00:04:00.740
potentially how significant is that?

00:04:00.740 --> 00:04:01.574
Some gift?

00:04:01.574 --> 00:04:03.843
Yeah, it's it's a boon to Iran.

00:04:03.843 --> 00:04:05.945
Iran is providing drones to Russia

00:04:06.112 --> 00:04:07.247
in return.

00:04:07.247 --> 00:04:08.948
They're getting systems

00:04:08.948 --> 00:04:10.483
so that they're reverse

00:04:10.483 --> 00:04:12.118
engineering and propagating

00:04:12.118 --> 00:04:12.852
throughout the region.

00:04:12.852 --> 00:04:13.853
They've done this before.

00:04:13.853 --> 00:04:15.989
Iran got a hold of the old TOW missile.

00:04:15.989 --> 00:04:18.725
They got a hold of old drones as well.

00:04:19.025 --> 00:04:21.561
So there's a Middle East regional impact

00:04:21.561 --> 00:04:23.796
if you now see advanced weapons

00:04:23.796 --> 00:04:25.398
being developed by Iran,

00:04:25.398 --> 00:04:26.499
and if they show themselves,

00:04:26.499 --> 00:04:27.300
for instance, with the tow

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:28.901
the ability to take one

00:04:28.901 --> 00:04:30.270
figure it out and make their own.

00:04:30.270 --> 00:04:31.638
Absolutely. That's alarming.

00:04:31.638 --> 00:04:31.838
Okay.

00:04:31.838 --> 00:04:33.206
Let's talk about the progress of war

00:04:33.206 --> 00:04:33.840
then.

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:34.374
In the U.S.,

00:04:34.374 --> 00:04:35.241
there's been a lot of talk

00:04:35.241 --> 00:04:37.910
about a Russian spring offensive

00:04:38.011 --> 00:04:39.212
really hasn't materialized.

00:04:39.212 --> 00:04:39.445
U.S.

00:04:39.445 --> 00:04:40.246
officials have been telling me

00:04:40.246 --> 00:04:40.713
for some time

00:04:40.713 --> 00:04:42.382
they just don't have the forces

00:04:42.382 --> 00:04:43.816
and the manpower

00:04:43.816 --> 00:04:45.318
to do anything definitive.

00:04:45.318 --> 00:04:46.019
But we also know

00:04:46.019 --> 00:04:48.288
Ukrainians want to carry out a counter

00:04:48.288 --> 00:04:49.889
offensive in the opposite direction.

00:04:49.889 --> 00:04:51.924
What is the actual state over here does?

00:04:51.924 --> 00:04:53.192
Does either side have the potential

00:04:53.192 --> 00:04:54.060
to make ground?

00:04:54.060 --> 00:04:54.394
Well,

00:04:54.394 --> 00:04:56.429
it really depends on what the Ukrainians

00:04:56.429 --> 00:04:57.930
have been doing over the winter time.

00:04:57.930 --> 00:04:58.231
Yes.

00:04:58.231 --> 00:05:00.033
We've been focusing on it,

00:05:00.033 --> 00:05:00.667
but hopefully

00:05:00.667 --> 00:05:01.901
they've been resupplying,

00:05:01.901 --> 00:05:04.470
rearming, retraining.

00:05:04.470 --> 00:05:06.606
They really have almost an imperative

00:05:06.606 --> 00:05:07.840
to have the spring offensive.

00:05:07.840 --> 00:05:08.775
They've got to demonstrate

00:05:08.775 --> 00:05:09.275
to the West

00:05:09.275 --> 00:05:10.610
that they're making progress

00:05:10.610 --> 00:05:12.078
that demonstrate to their own people

00:05:12.078 --> 00:05:13.313
that they're making progress.

00:05:13.313 --> 00:05:14.180
All the fighting,

00:05:14.180 --> 00:05:15.848
all the attention around back

00:05:15.848 --> 00:05:17.250
in these last several weeks.

00:05:17.250 --> 00:05:19.419
Extremely deadly for both sides.

00:05:19.419 --> 00:05:20.253
I mean, we're talking about

00:05:20.253 --> 00:05:22.755
some days where thousands are killed

00:05:22.755 --> 00:05:23.423
in a single.

00:05:23.423 --> 00:05:25.058
24 hour period.

00:05:25.058 --> 00:05:27.327
Has it been worth it for the Russians?

00:05:27.660 --> 00:05:29.228
But also crucially for the Ukrainians

00:05:29.228 --> 00:05:30.596
to fight so hard, so long

00:05:30.596 --> 00:05:31.831
and to give up so much there?

00:05:31.831 --> 00:05:32.598
I don't think so.

00:05:32.598 --> 00:05:33.766
I mean, retrospectively,

00:05:33.766 --> 00:05:35.468
this reminds me of World

00:05:35.468 --> 00:05:37.303
War One, these great battles

00:05:37.303 --> 00:05:38.671
where inches were gained

00:05:38.671 --> 00:05:39.972
and thousands were lost.

00:05:39.972 --> 00:05:40.373
Yeah.

00:05:40.373 --> 00:05:40.940
This is

00:05:40.940 --> 00:05:41.641
this is the area

00:05:41.641 --> 00:05:42.942
we're talking about here.

00:05:42.942 --> 00:05:44.344
So so what happens now

00:05:44.344 --> 00:05:45.411
in the coming weeks?

00:05:45.411 --> 00:05:45.945
You say

00:05:45.945 --> 00:05:47.280
that Ukraine has to make

00:05:47.280 --> 00:05:49.449
they have to make a push this way

00:05:49.716 --> 00:05:51.851
just to not be on their back foot,

00:05:51.851 --> 00:05:53.619
in effect.

00:05:53.619 --> 00:05:54.487
Do they make progress

00:05:54.487 --> 00:05:55.355
when they make that push?

00:05:55.355 --> 00:05:55.922
Well, first of all,

00:05:55.922 --> 00:05:56.389
I don't think

00:05:56.389 --> 00:05:57.890
that's where they're going to do it.

00:05:57.890 --> 00:05:59.992
If if I was advising them,

00:06:00.460 --> 00:06:02.829
I would be looking at a different area.

00:06:02.829 --> 00:06:05.465
There is a down here by Kherson

00:06:05.465 --> 00:06:07.567
going all the way up to 30 on.

00:06:08.101 --> 00:06:09.535
I think what they really want to try to

00:06:09.535 --> 00:06:12.372
do is unhinge the Russian offensive.

00:06:12.638 --> 00:06:13.873
Imagine if they were able

00:06:13.873 --> 00:06:15.842
to get all the way to Bernie ask

00:06:15.842 --> 00:06:16.275
they would

00:06:16.275 --> 00:06:18.444
essentially put all of Crimea

00:06:18.444 --> 00:06:19.712
at risk, particularly

00:06:19.712 --> 00:06:21.581
if the Americans put an attack on us.

00:06:21.581 --> 00:06:21.781
Right.

00:06:21.781 --> 00:06:22.882
And then the Russians

00:06:22.882 --> 00:06:23.783
are going to have to think

00:06:23.783 --> 00:06:25.418
about this land bridge

00:06:25.418 --> 00:06:26.853
that has been so important to them.

00:06:26.853 --> 00:06:27.954
How will they react.

00:06:27.954 --> 00:06:28.321
I mean that's

00:06:28.321 --> 00:06:29.722
been one of the principal goals

00:06:29.722 --> 00:06:31.991
of the whole Russian invasion is to join

00:06:32.158 --> 00:06:33.459
Russian controlled areas here

00:06:33.459 --> 00:06:35.261
with Crimea in the south.

00:06:35.261 --> 00:06:36.095
Great point.

00:06:36.095 --> 00:06:36.629
General Kimmitt,

00:06:36.629 --> 00:06:37.864
always good to have your expertize.

00:06:37.864 --> 00:06:38.398
Thank you.

00:06:38.398 --> 00:06:40.133
President Lynskey has been clear

00:06:40.133 --> 00:06:41.734
that this new tactic,

00:06:41.734 --> 00:06:42.769
no matter what it is,

00:06:42.769 --> 00:06:44.804
is still not going to make people

00:06:44.804 --> 00:06:45.271
stand down.

00:06:45.271 --> 00:06:45.938
I want you to take a

00:06:45.938 --> 00:06:47.006
listen to what he said about it.

00:06:50.476 --> 00:06:51.144
we have already

00:06:51.144 --> 00:06:53.179
shown what Ukraine is capable of.

00:06:53.346 --> 00:06:54.881
And no matter how treacherous

00:06:54.881 --> 00:06:56.449
Russia's actions are,

00:06:56.449 --> 00:06:57.150
Our state

00:06:57.150 --> 00:06:59.285
and people will not be in chains.

00:06:59.285 --> 00:07:00.153
Neither missiles

00:07:00.153 --> 00:07:00.820
nor of Russia's

00:07:00.820 --> 00:07:03.689
atrocities will help them.

00:07:03.689 --> 00:07:05.691
Now, Russia's defense ministry

00:07:05.691 --> 00:07:06.793
says this attack

00:07:06.793 --> 00:07:08.828
is retaliation, retaliation

00:07:09.028 --> 00:07:10.830
for an alleged cross-border attack

00:07:10.830 --> 00:07:12.532
in Verdansk that took place

00:07:12.532 --> 00:07:13.466
a few days ago.

00:07:13.466 --> 00:07:15.168
Ukraine has denied involvement

00:07:15.168 --> 00:07:16.002
in this attack.

00:07:16.002 --> 00:07:17.036
But I think it shows

00:07:17.036 --> 00:07:17.837
you it's

00:07:17.837 --> 00:07:20.039
a reflection of the Kremlin's thinking

00:07:20.106 --> 00:07:22.008
when retaliation looks like

00:07:22.008 --> 00:07:24.177
attacking civilian areas.

00:07:24.177 --> 00:07:25.144
And Sami, yesterday

00:07:25.144 --> 00:07:25.778
when you joined

00:07:25.778 --> 00:07:27.747
us, you mentioned how the ZAP region

00:07:27.747 --> 00:07:28.147
to power

00:07:28.147 --> 00:07:29.715
plant had been knocked off

00:07:29.715 --> 00:07:31.918
the power grid for the sixth time.

00:07:31.918 --> 00:07:33.186
I think in this conflict,

00:07:33.186 --> 00:07:35.054
obviously raising a lot of alarm

00:07:35.054 --> 00:07:36.422
among nuclear watchers.

00:07:36.422 --> 00:07:37.423
What more do we know

00:07:37.423 --> 00:07:38.391
about the safety of the plant

00:07:38.391 --> 00:07:39.192
at the moment?

00:07:39.192 --> 00:07:41.894
I think what really shook me is the quote

00:07:41.894 --> 00:07:42.728
from the head

00:07:42.728 --> 00:07:43.996
of the International Atomic

00:07:43.996 --> 00:07:44.831
Energy Agency.

00:07:44.831 --> 00:07:48.100
He said One day our luck will run out.

00:07:48.401 --> 00:07:49.702
And that is the concern, right?

00:07:49.702 --> 00:07:51.370
We're talking about a nuclear power plant

00:07:51.370 --> 00:07:52.872
right on the front lines

00:07:52.872 --> 00:07:54.574
that is Russian occupied,

00:07:54.574 --> 00:07:56.409
but run by Ukrainian engineers

00:07:56.409 --> 00:07:57.577
and Ukrainian staff

00:07:57.577 --> 00:07:59.512
that has over and over again

00:07:59.512 --> 00:08:01.681
been impacted by these massive missile

00:08:01.681 --> 00:08:03.649
attacks, by these massive strikes

00:08:03.649 --> 00:08:05.251
coming from Moscow

00:08:05.251 --> 00:08:06.786
The IAEA is saying, look,

00:08:06.786 --> 00:08:08.354
we have to do something about this.

00:08:08.354 --> 00:08:09.422
This is dangerous.

00:08:09.422 --> 00:08:11.324
This is something that is on the brink,

00:08:11.324 --> 00:08:12.992
that is absolutely unacceptable.

00:08:12.992 --> 00:08:14.460
And there's been several visits

00:08:14.460 --> 00:08:15.328
of course,

00:08:15.328 --> 00:08:16.929
by the nuclear watchdog,

00:08:16.929 --> 00:08:18.631
but that has yet to

00:08:18.631 --> 00:08:20.132
find a resolution to this.

00:08:20.132 --> 00:08:21.033
So you're still looking

00:08:21.033 --> 00:08:23.069
at Europe's largest nuclear power plant.

00:08:23.069 --> 00:08:23.369
That's what

00:08:23.369 --> 00:08:23.936
this Operation

00:08:23.936 --> 00:08:24.670
Nuclear Power Plant

00:08:24.670 --> 00:08:26.672
is caught in the crossfire

00:08:26.672 --> 00:08:27.807
with no solution

00:08:27.807 --> 00:08:30.610
as to how that plant can be stabilized

00:08:30.610 --> 00:08:31.978
and people can be certain

00:08:31.978 --> 00:08:33.513
that it doesn't become something worse

00:08:33.513 --> 00:08:33.913
and something

00:08:33.913 --> 00:08:35.615
running on emergency power, isn't it?

00:08:35.615 --> 00:08:37.483
So it's not completely out.

00:08:37.483 --> 00:08:38.317
Not completely out.

00:08:38.317 --> 00:08:39.852
It goes into blackout mode.

00:08:39.852 --> 00:08:41.220
So it's cut from the power grid.

00:08:41.220 --> 00:08:42.788
It goes into blackout mode.

00:08:42.788 --> 00:08:43.923
But you're still talking

00:08:43.923 --> 00:08:45.658
about a nuclear power plant. Right.

00:08:45.658 --> 00:08:47.193
There are serious concerns

00:08:47.193 --> 00:08:49.695
when you're talking about supplying power

00:08:49.695 --> 00:08:50.730
to a nuclear power plant

00:08:50.730 --> 00:08:53.466
and that supply not being stable

00:08:53.466 --> 00:08:54.901
not being reliable.

00:08:54.901 --> 00:08:56.002
Salma, thank you so much.

